1
00:02:47,647 --> 00:02:53,647
They tried to electrocute "Meat Cleaver" Max. It didn't work.

2
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:41,294
The Horror Show is a horror, thriller, fantasy film directed by James Isaac.

3
00:08:22,941 --> 00:08:28,941
Vowing revenge on the detective who apprehended him, serial killer "Meat Cleaver" Max
Jenke returns from beyond the grave to launch a whole new reign of terror.

4
00:11:10,588 --> 00:11:16,588
Detective Lucas McCarthy, played by Lance Henriksen.

5
00:13:58,235 --> 00:14:04,235
Max Jenke, played by Brion James.

6
00:16:45,882 --> 00:16:51,882
Donna McCarthy, played by Rita Taggart.

7
00:19:33,529 --> 00:19:39,529
Bonnie McCarthy, played by Dedee Pfeiffer.

8
00:22:21,176 --> 00:22:27,176
Scott McCarthy, played by Aron Eisenberg.

9
00:25:08,823 --> 00:25:14,823
Peter Campbell, played by Thom Bray.

10
00:27:56,470 --> 00:28:02,470
The Rocky Horror Picture Show is a 1975 independent musical comedy horror film produced by Lou
Adler and Michael White, directed by Jim Sharman, and distributed by 20th Century Fox.

11
00:30:44,117 --> 00:30:50,117
The screenplay was written by Sharman and Richard O'Brien,
who also played the supporting role Riff Raff.

12
00:33:31,764 --> 00:33:37,764
The film is based on the 1973 musical stage production The Rocky
Horror Show, with music, book, and lyrics by O'Brien.

13
00:36:19,411 --> 00:36:25,411
The production is a tribute to the science fiction and horror B
movies of the 1930s through to the early 1960s.

14
00:39:07,058 --> 00:39:13,058
The film stars Tim Curry (in his debut), Susan Sarandon, and Barry Bostwick.

15
00:41:54,705 --> 00:42:00,705
It is narrated by Charles Gray, with cast members from the original Royal Court Theatre, Roxy
Theatre, and Belasco Theatre productions, including Nell Campbell and Patricia Quinn.

16
00:44:42,352 --> 00:44:48,352
The story centres on a young engaged couple whose car breaks down in
the rain near a castle, where they search for help.

17
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
The castle is occupied by strangers in elaborate costumes holding a party.

18
00:50:17,647 --> 00:50:23,647
They then meet the head of the house, Dr.

19
00:53:05,294 --> 00:53:11,294
Frank-N-Furter, an apparently mad scientist and alien transvestite from the planet Transsexual
in the galaxy of Transylvania, who creates a living muscle man named Rocky.

20
00:55:52,941 --> 00:55:58,941
The film was shot in the United Kingdom at Bray Studios and on location at Oakley Court, a
country house best known for its earlier use by Hammer Film Productions.

21
00:58:40,588 --> 00:58:46,588
A number of props and set pieces were reused from the Hammer horror films.

22
01:01:28,235 --> 01:01:34,235
Although the film is both a parody of and tribute to many kitsch science fiction and horror
films, costume designer Sue Blane conducted no research for her designs.

23
01:04:15,882 --> 01:04:21,882
Blane has claimed that her creations for the film directly affected the development of punk
rock fashion trends, such as torn fishnet stockings and colourfully dyed hair.

24
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
Initially the film was largely ignored by critics, but it soon became a hit as a midnight movie, when
audiences began participating with the film at the Waverly Theater in New York City in 1976.

25
01:09:51,176 --> 01:09:57,176
Audience members returned to the cinemas frequently and talked back to the screen and began
dressing as the characters, spawning similar performance groups across the United States.

26
01:12:38,823 --> 01:12:44,823
At almost the same time, fans in costume began performing alongside the film.

27
01:15:26,470 --> 01:15:32,470
This "shadow cast" mimed the actions on screen, above and behind
them, while lip-synching their characters' lines.

28
01:18:14,117 --> 01:18:20,117
Still in limited release in 2026, 50 years after its premiere, it is
the longest-running theatrical release in film history.

29
01:21:01,764 --> 01:21:07,764
In many cities, live amateur shadow-casts act out the film as it is being shown
and heavily draw upon a tradition of audience participation.

30
01:23:49,411 --> 01:23:55,411
The film is most often shown close to Halloween.

31
01:26:37,058 --> 01:26:43,058
Today, the film has a large international cult following and has been
considered by many as one of the greatest musical films of all time.

32
01:29:24,705 --> 01:29:30,705
In 2005, it was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant."

33
01:32:12,352 --> 01:32:18,352
The tone is dark and intense.
